    "https://jobs.cortland.edu/postings/11814": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer - Physical Education",
      "description": "SUNY Cortland's Applicant Site | Adjunct Lecturer - Physical Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Home Student Employment Services CAS Employment Opportunities Adjunct Lecturer - Physical Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Budget Title Adjunct Lecturer Campus Title Adjunct Lecturer - Physical Education School/Division Academic Affairs, Division of Department Physical Education Faculty Sub-Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Level A0 Salary Range $5,500 per 3 credit hour course Salary Determination Position Effort Part-Time (enter FTE below) If Part-Time, enter FTE: FTE will be determined by the number of courses/placements assigned. Is this a temporary position? Yes If Temporary, enter End Date: Position Summary The Department of Physical Education at SUNY Cortland is accepting applications to fill potential part-time temporary teaching position openings for the 2026-2027 academic year. What makes SUNY Cortland a great place to work? • Our positions provide predictable salary progressions, and many offer permanency. • Generous benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance, various retirement program options, paid family leave and/or parental leaves, flexible spending and dependent care accounts, long term disability and tuition reimbursement. • SUNY Cortland prioritizes work-life balance and well-being in all forms. The university’s state-of-the-art Student Life Center is free for employees to use, with membership options for families. Alternate work schedules are available with a supervisor’s approval. • Professional development opportunities exist through training, continuing education programs, tuition reimbursement and conference travel, based on funding. • Cortland County and surrounding areas offer easy access to arts, entertainment, outdoor recreation and much more. Experience Cortland dives deep into the region’s offerings Major Responsibilities A classroom based 3 credit hour course pays $5500 per class. The department typically hires for the courses/subject areas listed below but this list is not all inclusive. Other courses/subject areas may become available within the department. ILLUSTRATIVE NEEDS INCLUDE : Activity/Theory Course Instructors Student Teacher Supervisors A classroom-based 3-credit hour course pays $5500 per class. A 1-credit hour activity course pays $1833 per class. Student Teacher Supervisors must have experience teaching physical education. Functional and Supervisory Relationships Required Qualifications Appropriate level of experience and/or Master’s degree. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree preferred. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities About the University EEO Statement SUNY is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants, including individuals with disabilities. Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application, interview, or hiring process may request an accommodation by contacting our HR ADA Coordinator in Miller Room 302, 607-753-2302, hr@cortland.edu. Requests for accommodation will be considered consistent with applicable law. This process is separate from, and does not require, any voluntary self-identification of disability status. Job Close Date 10/19/2027 Posting Detail Information Posting Number F26023 Review Start Date 12/31/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://jobs.cortland.edu/postings/11796 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Professional References Contact Info. ONLY (minimum of 3) Human Resources P.O. Box 2000 Cortland, NY 13045 607-753-2302 HR@cortland.edu © SUNY Cortland> To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
